    <title>Communications routes authorize the exact record they act on: send and send-bulk, template render, archive, suggest-associations, confirm-affinity, status, record threads, ad-hoc create-task, proposal dismiss and create-task/apply, and account verify check the caller's OWN Dataverse rights before any app-only read or write (route authorization sweep 2026-10-02, owner round 9)</title>
    <phase>Session 27 — route authorization sweep (owner round 9, 2026-10-03)</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Authorization-path .cs change on live, unconditionally mapped BFF routes (tags bff-api, auth, security). Closes two critical disclosures (any document's file bytes emailed to any address; any column of any record rendered into a template) plus app-only writes onto records the caller cannot see.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Twelve route keys across two endpoint files, each with a different resource kind (route communication id, route proposal id, route account id, body document ids, body thread id, body regarding records, body template id) and a different right (Read, Write, AppendTo, a table Create or Assign privilege). Each must authorize exactly the id its handler consumes, keep unknown and denied ids indistinguishable, and leave the system callers of the same services (registration email, AI email disposition, the Job B/C apply paths) unaffected.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
