  <prompt>Every /api/communications route below checks only that the caller is signed in, then reads or writes, as the BFF's own identity, a record the caller chose. Make each route ask Dataverse, as the caller, about the exact record it is about to read, attach to, or change, before it touches that record. Deny unknown and denied ids with the same answer. Do not put the check inside the shared services, because system callers use them with no user.</prompt>

  <amendments source="main session, 2026-10-03, owner rounds 9-10" binding="true">
    <!-- Read these before step 0. Each overrides anything below that contradicts it. -->
    <amendment>Owner decisions now run to round 10: re-read notes/session27-owner-decisions-and-research.md rounds 9 and 10 on work/unified-access-control-r2 before step 0. They are newer than this POML.</amendment>
    <amendment>Do NOT rename or move FinanceAuthorizationFilter, and do not create a RecordAccessAuthorizationFilter or any other generalized copy of it: reuse it as it is. The rename is follow-up task 170, after the sweep tasks are integrated. Several sweep tasks reuse this filter in parallel, and a move in one of them would conflict with all the others.</amendment>
    <amendment>Task 167 (the every-route guard) runs IN PARALLEL with this task. If RouteAuthorizationGuardTests on your branch has no Pending waiver for your routes (167 not yet landed), do NOT add waivers, ledger entries or Permanent waivers, and do NOT add your files to GovernedFiles. Instead, add a table "Route authorization ledger input" to your task note, with one row per route you changed or deleted: the route key exactly as the guard spells it (VERB /path), the mechanism that now decides (filter, probe or impersonation), the deny test (its fully qualified name, proving a caller without rights is refused), and, for a list whose query runs AS the caller, the words "handler decision: query runs as the caller". The main session records these in 167's ledger at integration. If 167 HAS landed on your branch, follow its ledger contract: delete your Pending waivers and set ResolvedBy and ProofTest in the same diff.</amendment>
    <amendment>Owner round 10 item 1 (BINDING): delete a route when it has NO caller in the repo AND it is NOT in any published API description; fix it otherwise. Search the repo for OpenAPI documents and Copilot or agent plugin manifests (for example *openapi*, ai-plugin*, *manifest*.json, declarativeAgent*) before you decide. List every deletion, with its no-caller and not-published evidence, in the note and the PR. Delete the services, filters and options that only the deleted routes used. Keep the file census count in RouteAuthorizationGuardTests right if a whole endpoint file goes.</amendment>
    <amendment>Impersonation: never assign ServiceClient.CallerId or CallerAADObjectId outside Spaarke.Dataverse/DataverseImpersonation.cs (task 160 adds the single SDK entry point there, plus an arch rule). For the Web API, impersonate through DataverseWebApiService's existing impersonateSystemUserId parameter (MSCRMCallerID). It refuses Guid.Empty (task 104).</amendment>
    <amendment>Also in scope (no deferral): thread rename, pin and deactivate, and message deactivate (CommunicationEndpoints.cs, about lines 165/178/192/204). They gate on Read and then write app-only. A write to the shared thread or message record requires WRITE on that record (owner D1). If a Read-only Direct-thread participant then loses pinning, record it in the note as a behaviour change. Do NOT weaken the Write requirement.</amendment>
    <amendment>Suggestions Status, AutoFileEligible and the per-candidate Conflict flag are recomputed over the TRIMMED candidate set, so the response infers nothing about hidden candidates.</amendment>
  </amendments>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer — BFF authorization filters and the communication read seams. Expert in ASP.NET Core Minimal API endpoint filters (ADR-008), ProblemDetails (ADR-019), Dataverse RetrievePrincipalAccess over OBO, and impersonated (MSCRMCallerID) Web API reads. Fail closed (ADR-003).</role>

  <goal>After this task, for each route key in the acceptance criteria (the twelve sweep-finding keys: send, send-bulk, template/render, archive, suggest-associations, confirm-affinity, status, POST threads, ad-hoc create-task, proposal create-task/apply, proposal dismiss, accounts verify; plus the three routes that share a proposal or communication key: proposal apply, proposal undo, tasks/{taskId}/undo):
(1) the route decides, as the caller and before any app-only Dataverse read that returns data to the caller, any SPE download, any Graph call, and any Dataverse or SPE write, whether the caller holds the right named for that route on the record the handler consumes;
(2) a caller without that right gets the route's deny answer, and an id that does not exist gets the byte-identical answer (apart from trace and correlation ids);
(3) a caller with the right gets the same result as today;
(4) the check is an endpoint filter in each route's own fluent chain, visible to RouteAuthorizationGuardTests, and is never placed inside CommunicationService, ThreadResolver, CommunicationCreateTaskApplyService, CommunicationProposalApplyService, AffinityConfirmationRecorder, MailboxVerificationService or EmailTemplateService;
(5) the suggest-associations response and the Office suggestions response carry no candidate the caller cannot read;
(6) the behaviour is proven live in dev by the main session with a non-admin test user.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>🔴 LIVE. Every anchor below was read against the working tree of branch work/unified-access-control-r2 at b18a7d321 on 2026-10-02. Line numbers drift; re-verify each before editing.

WHY "SIGNED IN" IS ALL THERE IS TODAY.
- `Api/CommunicationEndpoints.cs:51-53` maps the `/api/communications` group with a bare `.RequireAuthorization()`. The BFF registers no DefaultPolicy or FallbackPolicy (`Infrastructure/DI/AuthorizationModule.cs` registers named policies only), so that means "authenticated".
- `Api/Filters/CommunicationAuthorizationFilter.cs:13-43` checks `IsAuthenticated` and that an oid claim resolves, then calls `next`. Its own summary says "Phase 1: Any authenticated user with a valid identity can send."
- `tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.cs:1211-1215` lists it in `ClaimOnlyFilters` with the reason "Per-record scoping is ICommunicationAccessFilter's job". That premise is false for every route in this task: none of their paths calls `ICommunicationAccessFilter`.
- Neither `Api/CommunicationEndpoints.cs` nor `Api/CommunicationTemplateEndpoints.cs` is in `GovernedFiles` (`RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.cs:126-`), so the guard does not see these routes at all.
- Both files are mapped unconditionally: `Infrastructure/DI/EndpointMappingExtensions.cs:363` (`MapCommunicationEndpoints`) and `:368` (`MapCommunicationTemplateEndpoints`).
- Every read and write below goes through `IGenericEntityService`, which is the app-only `IDataverseService` singleton (`Infrastructure/DI/GraphModule.cs:97`), or through Graph/SPE with `ForApp()`. Dataverse row security, secure isolation and the No Access list therefore do not apply to the caller.
- Several route descriptions say "Auth-scoped via the endpoint filter (NFR-07)" (suggest-associations `:250`, confirm-affinity comment `:255-261`). That is the misdescription the sweep's "noteworthy" line flags.

THE ROUTES (the verified findings, one per entry of idor-group-161.json; eleven entries, twelve route keys because send and send-bulk are two keys).
- `POST /api/communications/template/render` — `Api/CommunicationTemplateEndpoints.cs:38-45` (app-level MapPost, `.RequireAuthorization()` only, no filter). Handler `RenderTemplateAsync` `:55-130`. `FetchRegardingVariablesAsync` `:138-185` builds `QueryExpression(request.RegardingEntityType)` with `ColumnSet(true)` on `{entityType}id == RegardingRecordId` (`:152-160`) through the app-only service. The entity type is free text with no allow-list. Every attribute becomes a merge variable through `UnwrapDataverseValue` (`:188-195`: OptionSetValue → its integer, EntityReference → its Name, Money → its decimal, other values as-is), and the rendered subject and body go back to the caller. The template is fetched app-only by a caller-chosen `TemplateId` (`Services/Ai/Delivery/EmailTemplateService.cs:128-150`, URL `templates({templateId})?$select=...` at `:141`), with no `ispersonal` or owner check; a missing template returns `EmailTemplateResult.Fail("Email template not found: {templateId}")` (`:60`), which the handler turns into 404 title "Template Not Found" (`:113-122`). The catch at `:175-182` swallows read failures, and a missing record renders empty. Severity CRITICAL.
- `POST /api/communications/send` (`:55-62`, handler `:420-429`) and `POST /api/communications/send-bulk` (`:64-72`, handler `:536-666`, which builds one `SendCommunicationRequest` per recipient at `:592-605`, copying `AttachmentDocumentIds` and `Associations`; `BulkSendRequest` has no `ThreadId` and no `InheritRegardingFromCommunicationId`). `SendCommunicationRequest` (`Services/Communication/Models/SendCommunicationRequest.cs`): `Associations` `:59`, `SendMode` `:71`, `AttachmentDocumentIds` (a `string[]`, not Guids) `:88`, `InheritRegardingFromCommunicationId` `:108`, `ThreadId` `:122`. `CommunicationService.SendAsync` (`Services/Communication/CommunicationService.cs:1040`) has three branches: Message (`:1058-1061` → `SendMessageAsync` `:600`), SendMode.User (`:1064-1067` → `SendAsUserAsync` `:1402`) and shared mailbox (`:1069-`).
  - Attachments: the two EMAIL branches (shared mailbox `:1076`, User `:1429`) resolve each `AttachmentDocumentIds` entry through the app-only `IDocumentDataverseService` (`:2467`) and download it in `DownloadAndBuildAttachmentsAsync` (`:2424-`) with `SpeFileStore.DownloadFileAsync`, which uses `ForApp()`. The cap is `MaxAttachmentCount = 150` (`:2409`, enforced as a 400 `ATTACHMENT_LIMIT_EXCEEDED` at `:2430-2443`); a missing document is a 404 `ATTACHMENT_NOT_FOUND` today. The Message branch does not download attachments.
  - ThreadId: consumed only on the Message branch (`:936-938` → `AssignExplicitThreadAsync` `:992-1029`), which stamps the thread app-only and then calls `GrantMessageAccessAsync` for that thread's participants.
  - InheritRegardingFromCommunicationId: read app-only and its regarding lookups copied by `CopyRegardingFromSourceAsync` (`:2002-`), on all three branches (`:870-871`, `:1784-1785`, `:1889-1890`).
  - Associations: `MapAssociationFieldsAsync` (`:1928-1991`) writes `Associations[0]` into a typed regarding lookup through `RegardingLookupMap` (`:1908-1922`, case-insensitive) and writes the denormalized id, name and url text even for an unmapped type.
  The caller chooses all four and the To/Cc/Bcc addresses. Severity CRITICAL: any signed-in user can email the bytes of any sprk_document, secure ones included, to any external address.
- `POST /api/communications/{id:guid}/archive` (`:239-245`, handler `:713-720`, no caller passed) → `ArchiveExistingAsync` (`CommunicationService.cs:214-`): app-only read of subject, from, to, cc and body (a missing row is a 404 `COMMUNICATION_NOT_FOUND`, `:226-234`), app-only creation of sprk_document rows that each carry `sprk_relatedcommunication` (`:479`, `:2163`, `:2341`), an SPE upload, and an AI analysis enqueue. Severity HIGH.
- `POST /api/communications/{id:guid}/suggest-associations` (`:247-253`, handler `:984-993`, no caller passed) → `ReconstructEnvelopeAsync` (`CommunicationService.cs:340-`, app-only; a missing row is a 404 `COMMUNICATION_NOT_FOUND`, `:361-369`) → `IncomingAssociationResolver.EvaluateAsync`. The response (`Services/Communication/Models/SuggestAssociationsResponse.cs`) returns each candidate's `TargetEntity`, `TargetId`, confidences and contributor provenance, plus `Status`, `AutoFileEligible` and `Signals`. Severity HIGH.
- `POST /api/communications/{communicationId:guid}/create-task` (`:347-355`, handler `:1083-1100`) → `CommunicationCreateTaskApplyService.CreateAdHocAsync` (`Services/Communication/CommunicationCreateTaskApplyService.cs:425-`). Its comment (`:442-444`) says association gating is the UI's. `IActionSeam.CreateTaskAsync` (`:475`) creates the sprk_event app-only with a caller-chosen `RegardingEntity`/`RegardingRecordId` and `OwnerId = request.AssignedTo` (`:483`). `TaskActionCore` (`Services/Ai/Nodes/ActionCore/TaskActionCore.cs`) writes `ownerid` from `OwnerId` (`:191-192`), and for a regarding type outside its `RegardingFieldByEntity` map (`:85-101`, which also accepts `sprk_communication` and `sprk_recordtype_ref`) it still creates the task with no regarding (`:181-188`). Only the later FR-E5 PATCH is impersonated. Nothing checks that the communication exists. Severity HIGH.
- `POST /api/communications/proposals/{reviewLogId:guid}/create-task/apply` (`:329-337`, handler `:1068-1077`) → `ApplyAsync` (`:230-`): the sprk_emailreviewlog row is loaded app-only (`LoadReviewLogRowAsync` `:677`; a missing row is a 404 `PROPOSAL_NOT_FOUND`, `:247-255`), and the sprk_event is created app-only (`:328`) regarding the proposal's `sprk_targetentity`/`sprk_targetrecordid`, owned by the caller-chosen `request.AssignedTo`. Nothing checks the caller can see the proposal's communication or attach to the target. Severity MEDIUM.
- `POST /api/communications/proposals/{reviewLogId:guid}/dismiss` (`:310-318`, handler `:1054-1062`) → `CommunicationProposalApplyService.DismissAsync` (`Services/Communication/CommunicationProposalApplyService.cs:347-`): app-only row load (`LoadReviewLogRowAsync` `:563`), app-only Dismissed audit row. The response echoes target entity and field. Severity MEDIUM.
- `POST /api/communications/{id:guid}/confirm-affinity` (`:262-266`, handler `:1009-1017`) → `AffinityConfirmationRecorder.RecordAsync` (`Services/Communication/Engine/AffinityConfirmationRecorder.cs:49-101`): validates only that the target type is ADR-024-mapped, reads the communication app-only, and writes affinity frequencies app-only. It NEVER fails: every no-op, including a non-existent communication id (the envelope read throws and the catch returns 0), answers 200 `RecordAffinityConfirmationResult(RecordedSignals: 0)` (`Services/Communication/Models/RecordAffinityConfirmation.cs:20`). Affinity is on by default, with 3 confirmations to plant a suggestion. Severity MEDIUM (learning-signal poisoning). The only client is fire-and-forget and swallows failures (`src/client/shared/Spaarke.Communication.Components/src/components/EmailWorkspace/EmailWorkspace.tsx:446`); it is called only AFTER `applyRegardingSelection` has written the target into the communication's typed `sprk_regarding*` lookup (`EmailAssociationsAndTracking/EmailConnectionsReview.tsx:163-176`, `logic/connections/ConnectionsWriteHandler.ts:205-244`).
- `POST /api/communications/accounts/{id:guid}/verify` (`:384-389`, handler `:1128-1145`) → `MailboxVerificationService.VerifyAsync` (`Services/Communication/MailboxVerificationService.cs:57-`): app-only read and update of sprk_communicationaccount (`:261`, `:289`), Graph `ForApp()` test send, inbox read and subscription create (`:166`, `:218`, `:339`). A missing account is a null result, which the handler turns into 404 `ACCOUNT_NOT_FOUND` (`:1135-1142`). An operator action with no operator gate. Severity MEDIUM.
- `GET /api/communications/{id:guid}/status` (`:74-78`) has NO endpoint filter at all. Handler `:668-711` takes no caller and reads statuscode, sprk_graphmessageid, sprk_sentat and sprk_from app-only; any retrieve failure is a 404 `COMMUNICATION_NOT_FOUND` (`:683-690`). 404 versus 200 is an existence oracle. Severity LOW.
- `POST /api/communications/threads` (`:109-115`, handler `:488-524`) → `ThreadResolver.CreateRecordThreadAsync` (`Services/Communication/ThreadResolver.cs:409-465`): validates only the regarding type (`RegardingFieldMap.FieldFor`, `:433-436`, which throws ArgumentException for an unmapped type) and that the id parses, then creates the thread app-only with the typed regarding lookup and the caller-supplied `RegardingRecordName` (`:458-459`), which also becomes the thread name when no name is given (`:418-421`). The handler passes `request.RegardingRecordName` into `RecordThreadAnchor` (`:517-520`). This bypasses AppendTo on the regarding record and lets the caller set the displayed record name. Severity MEDIUM.

FOLDED IN. `GET /api/office/communications/by-message-id/{internetMessageId}/suggestions` (`Api/Office/CommunicationsEndpoints.cs:372-399`) resolves candidate NAMES through the delegated client (`ResolveCandidateNamesAsync`, `:426-`) and leaves unreadable candidates nameless, but returns `Suggestions = suggestions` (`:397`) unfiltered, so their ids still go back. Task 127's criterion "The suggestions response contains no candidate the caller cannot read — neither name nor id" is not met by the code. It is the same disclosure as suggest-associations, so one trimming helper fixes both.

WHO ELSE CALLS THE SAME SERVICES (why the check belongs at the endpoint). `CommunicationService.SendAsync` is also called with no HttpContext by `Services/Registration/RegistrationEmailService.cs:75, :116, :162, :201, :237, :271`, and by `Services/Ai/EmailDispositionSender.cs:107`. `ReconstructEnvelopeAsync` is also called by `CommunicationCreateTaskApplyService.cs:313`, `CommunicationProposalApplyService.cs:259`, `AffinityConfirmationRecorder.cs:69` and the Office suggestions route. A caller check inside these services would break the registration emails or tempt an app-only fallback.

LIVE CLIENTS (each must keep working for an authorized user):
- send: `src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/services/communicationApi.ts:275`, `EntityCreationService.ts:819-828`, `communicationTimelineApi.ts:349`, the CommunicationTimeline and CommunicationMessageActions PCFs.
- template render: `src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/EmailComposer/createXrmEmailComposeHandlers.ts:318` (throws on any non-OK; it lists templates through the caller's own Xrm.WebApi, so a listed template is readable by the caller).
- archive: `src/client/pcf/CommunicationActions/CommunicationActions/CommunicationActionsApp.tsx:523`.
- confirm-affinity: `EmailWorkspace.tsx:446`.
- proposals: `src/client/shared/Spaarke.Communication.Components/src/components/ReconcileTabs/FieldUpdateReconcileTab.tsx:484` (apply), `:508` (undo), `:526` (dismiss); `TaskReconcileTab.tsx:383` and `:479` (ad-hoc create-task), `:395` (create-task/apply), `:387` and `:446` (dismiss). TaskReconcileTab sends `assignedTo` in the create-task bodies.
- threads: `src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/services/communicationThreadListApi.ts:454`.
- verify: `docs/guides/COMMUNICATION-ADMIN-GUIDE.md:145` and `:447` describe a "Verify" button on the Communication Account form and direct use of the endpoint; no caller was found in src.

EXISTING ACCESS MACHINERY TO REUSE (read each before writing code):
- Communication visibility, as the caller: `Services/Communication/CommunicationThreadReadService.cs` — `CanCallerSeeThreadAsync` (`:779-785`) and `CanCallerSeeMessageAsync` (`:793-799`) run one impersonated top-1 query through `IImpersonatedCommunicationQuery` and refuse an unresolved caller with a 403 `THREAD_READ_FORBIDDEN` (`ResolveCallerOrThrowAsync`, `:733-751`). `CanCallerSeeMessageAsync` does NOT apply the internal-only and privilege rules; the read paths do, by selecting `InternalOnlyField` (`:75`) and `PrivilegeField` and calling `ICommunicationAccessFilter` (`Services/Communication/Access/ICommunicationAccessFilter.cs`: `EvaluateMessage(CommunicationAccessContext, Entity)`) with a `CommunicationAccessContext` built from `ISystemUserIdentityResolver.IsExternalAsync` — see `GetUnreadCountAsync` (`:207-236`) for the exact sequence. Entity-set constants: `CommunicationSet = "sprk_communications"` (`:39`), `ThreadSet = "sprk_communicationthreads"` (`:41`).
- Impersonated reads of ANY table: `Services/Communication/IImpersonatedCommunicationQuery.cs` — `QueryAsync(entitySetName, odataQuery, callerSystemUserId, ct)`, implemented by `DataverseWebApiService.RetrieveMultipleImpersonatedAsync` (`src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/DataverseWebApiService.cs:1030-1066`): MSCRMCallerID impersonation, refuses `Guid.Empty`, throws on a non-success status (`EnsureSuccessStatusCode`), and ALREADY sends `Prefer: odata.include-annotations="OData.Community.Display.V1.FormattedValue"` (`:1051-1060`), so a lookup's display name rides the same row. Registered unconditionally (`Infrastructure/DI/CommunicationModule.cs:279`). This is the round-9 "existing DataverseImpersonation helper".
- The proposal visibility rule already in force: `Services/Communication/CommunicationQueueFeedService.cs:28-36` and `:133-162` — a proposal is shown to a caller only when its parent communication passes the impersonated read plus the shared access filter; the review-log lookup itself is app-only but scoped to communication ids already proven visible.
- Record rights and privileges, as the caller: `Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/CallerRecordAccessProbe.cs` — `GetCallerRightsAsync(callerBearerToken, entitySet, recordId, ct)` (`:212-`, OBO WhoAmI plus RetrievePrincipalAccess, `AccessRights.None` on every fault), `GetCallerRightsForRecordsAsync(callerBearerToken, targets, ct)` (`:274-`, many records, one identity lookup, at most 4 concurrent), `CallerHoldsPrivilegeAsync(callerBearerToken, privilegeName, ct)` (`:386-`, uncached, false on every fault; added by task 130). All three are `virtual`, so tests substitute them. Registered unconditionally (`Infrastructure/DI/ExternalAccessModule.cs:122`). Note the ~1.6 s not-found backoff `NotFoundRetryDelay` (`:101-`) that also lands on genuine denials.
- Rights to operation mapping: `src/server/shared/Spaarke.Core/Auth/OperationAccessPolicy.cs` — `"read"` = Read (`:163`), `"write"` = Write (`:242`), `"entity.associate_document"` = AppendTo (`:213`, named for documents), `HasRequiredRights(AccessRights, string)` (`:320`).
- Document rights (the same decision the document download routes make): `Api/Filters/DocumentAuthorizationFilter.cs:75-100` builds an `AuthorizationContext { UserId, ResourceId, Operation, UserAccessToken }` and calls `AuthorizationService.AuthorizeAsync` (`src/server/shared/Spaarke.Core/Auth/AuthorizationService.cs:28`). The download-family routes use operation `"read"` (`Api/FileAccessEndpoints.cs:61`).
- Delegated (OBO) reads: `Infrastructure/Dataverse/IDataverseUserClient.cs:56-` (`GetAsync(relativePath, ct)`, no app-only fallback, fails with `DataverseUserClientErrorCodes.UserContextRequired` `:155`). Task 127's reference use: `Api/Office/CommunicationsEndpoints.cs:426-` `ResolveCandidateNamesAsync`, which treats a non-success response as "not readable" and drops that candidate's name.
- Entity-set and primary-name map: `Services/Communication/RegardingNameFields.cs` — `PrimaryNameField` (`:15-29`) and `EntitySetName` (`:50-63`), both case-SENSITIVE switches. Its remarks (`:46-47`) say `RegardingNameFieldsTests` pins that the two key sets agree, but no such test exists (a search of tests/ for RegardingNameFields finds nothing). It covers matter, project, invoice, event, work assignment, service request, budget, analysis (`sprk_analyses`), organization, contact and account. It does NOT cover `sprk_reportcard`, which `Services/Communication/Engine/RegardingFieldMap.cs:13-27` (case-insensitive) treats as an ADR-024 regarding family. `CommunicationService.RegardingLookupMap` (`:1908-1922`) carries a second, UNUSED entity-set column that says `sprk_analysises` for sprk_analysis; it disagrees with RegardingNameFields and must not be used.
- The finance precedent this task copies: task 130 (`tasks/130-c8-finance-recalculate-idor-and-summary-gate.poml`, `Api/Filters/FinanceAuthorizationFilter.cs`) — a per-route declaration of which id is authorized, from which source (route or body), for which right; endpoint filter in the fluent chain; uniform 404 for unknown and denied route ids; body-id denials as 403; the G5 "check as the user, write as the app" pattern with `CallerHoldsPrivilegeAsync` for a table privilege.

GUARD STATE. `RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.cs` — `ExplicitlyCreditedFilterTypeNames` (`:1886-1896`); `FilterMarker` (`:1898-1902`) credits any `.Add*AuthorizationFilter(` call and any `AddEndpointFilter&lt;*Authorization*Filter&gt;` or `*Access*Filter`; Rule B (`NoAuthorizationFilterIsDecorative`, `:1107-`) requires every `*AuthorizationFilter.cs` file to contain one of the `DecisionServices` strings (`:1275-1302`: `AuthorizationService`, `IAccessDataSource`, `AccessRights`, `RetrievePrincipalAccess`, `ICommunicationAccessFilter`, `CallerRecordAccessProbe`, among others) unless it is in `ClaimOnlyFilters`. `IImpersonatedCommunicationQuery`, `CommunicationThreadReadService` and `IDataverseUserClient` are NOT in `DecisionServices`. Because `CommunicationAuthorizationFilter` matches `FilterMarker` and is claim-only, today's Rule A would count every route here as gated: the current guard cannot tell the fix from the hole. Task 167 extends the guard to every route file and adds a Pending waiver, owned by this task, for each finding route; this task deletes those waivers as it fixes the routes. Task 167 had NOT landed on this branch when this POML was authored (no 167 POML exists; neither file is in GovernedFiles; no waiver names task 161) — the main session reconciles the waivers at integration if it still has not landed when this task runs.</background>
