  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-003">Scope: every route in this task. Fail closed. A missing caller oid, a missing bearer token, an unresolved Dataverse systemuser, a failed OBO exchange, a RetrievePrincipalAccess or impersonated-query fault, a privilege-check fault, or any exception in a check DENIES. There is no app-only fallback on any path. An authorization fault is never turned into a success or into "no data". A deny for a reason that does not depend on the id (no token, unresolved caller) may use the existing 403 (for example `THREAD_READ_FORBIDDEN` from `ResolveCallerOrThrowAsync`); every deny that depends on the id uses the route's deny answer below.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner round 9">Scope: every route in this task. An id that does not exist and an id the caller may not use get the same answer, byte-identical apart from trace and correlation ids.
- ROUTE ids (communication id, proposal id, account id): the route's existing not-found body — `COMMUNICATION_NOT_FOUND` 404 (status, archive, suggest-associations), `PROPOSAL_NOT_FOUND` 404 (the four proposal routes), `ACCOUNT_NOT_FOUND` 404 (verify) — reproduced exactly (same status, title, detail text and code). A 403 for "exists but denied" on a route id would be an existence oracle.
- Routes with no not-found answer today: ad-hoc create-task and tasks/{taskId}/undo use the `COMMUNICATION_NOT_FOUND` 404 body that archive uses. confirm-affinity keeps its "never fails" contract (NFR-04): every deny answers 200 `RecordedSignals: 0`, which is exactly what a non-existent communication id answers today.
- BODY ids (attachments, thread, inherit-from communication, associations, regarding records, template regarding): a 403 with ONE reasonCode per route, byte-identical for unknown, denied and unparseable ids. Use reasonCodes of the form `sdap.access.deny.communication.{route}` (`.send`, `.send_bulk`, `.template_render`, `.thread_create`, `.create_task`, `.archive`) through `ProblemDetailsHelper.Forbidden` (ADR-019).
- The template id: an unreadable template gets the response a non-existent template gets today: 404, title "Template Not Found", detail "Email template not found: {templateId}".</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: placement. Each check is an ENDPOINT FILTER attached in the route's own fluent chain (ADR-008) through ONE extension method, `.AddCommunicationRecordAuthorizationFilter(...)`, which is textually distinct from the bare identity filter `.AddEndpointFilter&lt;CommunicationAuthorizationFilter&gt;()`. On routes that carry the identity filter today it stays and runs FIRST; the record filter is added after it. The record filter reads body ids from the bound request argument (as FinanceAuthorizationFilter does), never by re-reading the request stream. NEVER put a caller check inside CommunicationService, ThreadResolver, CommunicationCreateTaskApplyService, CommunicationProposalApplyService, TaskActionCore, AffinityConfirmationRecorder, MailboxVerificationService or EmailTemplateService — RegistrationEmailService and EmailDispositionSender call SendAsync with no HttpContext, and the Job B/C paths call ReconstructEnvelopeAsync. The route HANDLERS in CommunicationEndpoints.cs, CommunicationTemplateEndpoints.cs and Office/CommunicationsEndpoints.cs may read as the caller (template merge read, thread record name, candidate trimming); those reads are not the gate and do not replace the filter.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: the rights each route requires (decided at authoring; the escalation triggers name the ones that need the owner if the live gate disagrees).
- COMMUNICATION VISIBILITY (used below): the impersonated top-1 read of the communication returns the row AND `ICommunicationAccessFilter.EvaluateMessage` says visible (internal-only and privilege rules). Add ONE method to CommunicationThreadReadService that does exactly this, following `GetUnreadCountAsync`'s sequence; do not change `CanCallerSeeMessageAsync` (DELETE /{id} depends on it).
- status, suggest-associations, tasks/{taskId}/undo: communication visibility on the route id.
- PROPOSAL VISIBILITY (dismiss, create-task/apply, Job B apply, Job B undo): load the sprk_emailreviewlog row's `sprk_communication` lookup (app-only, as the queue feed does; the value is not returned to the caller), then communication visibility. A missing row, a row with no communication and an invisible communication give the identical `PROPOSAL_NOT_FOUND` 404.
- archive: communication visibility, AND AppendTo on the communication (the created sprk_document rows carry `sprk_relatedcommunication`), AND the caller holds the Create privilege on sprk_document (`CallerHoldsPrivilegeAsync`).
- confirm-affinity: communication visibility, AND the impersonated read of the communication shows its typed regarding lookup for `targetEntityType` (RegardingFieldMap) equal to `targetRecordId`, AND the caller holds Write on the communication. When any of these fails the route returns 200 `RecordedSignals: 0` and AffinityStore is never called.
- ad-hoc create-task: communication visibility on the route id, AND AppendTo on the body regarding record, AND the Create privilege on sprk_event. A regarding type with no entity set in RegardingNameFields (for example `sprk_communication` or `sprk_recordtype_ref`, which TaskActionCore accepts) is DENIED with the route's 403, not guessed.
- create-task/apply: proposal visibility, AND AppendTo on the proposal's `sprk_targetentity`/`sprk_targetrecordid`, AND the Create privilege on sprk_event.
- ASSIGN (both create-task routes): while TaskActionCore on this task's branch writes `ownerid` from `OwnerId = request.AssignedTo` (`TaskActionCore.cs:191-192`), a request whose AssignedTo is present and is not the caller's own systemuserid additionally requires the caller's Assign privilege on sprk_event (`CallerHoldsPrivilegeAsync`). If task 146 has landed and ownerid no longer comes from AssignedTo, do not add this check, and record which case applied in the task note. This task does not decide ownership.
- threads (POST): AppendTo on the body regarding record. The handler passes, as `RecordThreadAnchor.RecordName`, that record's primary name (`RegardingNameFields.PrimaryNameField`) read AS THE CALLER through `IImpersonatedCommunicationQuery`; the body `RegardingRecordName` is never persisted and never names the thread. ThreadResolver is not modified. A regarding type with no entity set in RegardingNameFields → 400 `VALIDATION_ERROR` before any Dataverse call.
- send and send-bulk: every AttachmentDocumentIds entry passes `AuthorizationService.AuthorizeAsync` with Operation `"read"` (the decision the document download route makes; a reader can already download the bytes, so emailing them adds no capability); ThreadId passes `CanCallerSeeThreadAsync`; InheritRegardingFromCommunicationId passes communication visibility; every Associations entry, AND every regarding record that would be copied from the inherit-from communication (its populated `RegardingFieldMap.AllRegardingFields` lookups, read as the caller), has AppendTo. The filter checks every id the body carries, on every CommunicationType and SendMode, once per request, before the first SendAsync. An attachment id that does not parse as a GUID gets the same 403. More than 150 attachment ids (CommunicationService `MaxAttachmentCount`) gets today's 400 `ATTACHMENT_LIMIT_EXCEEDED` before any rights query. Recipients, FromMailbox and SendMode are unchanged by this task.
- template render: RegardingEntityType must be a key of `RegardingNameFields.EntitySetName` (otherwise 400 before any Dataverse call); the caller must hold Read on the regarding record (`CallerRecordAccessProbe.GetCallerRightsAsync`); the template must be readable by the caller (impersonated top-1 read of the `templates` entity set by `templateid`). The handler then reads the regarding record for the merge AS THE CALLER through `IImpersonatedCommunicationQuery` (so Dataverse applies row AND field-level security), never through IGenericEntityService. The template body fetch inside EmailTemplateService stays as it is (G5: checked as the user, then read as the app).
- accounts verify: Write on the sprk_communicationaccount record (the action overwrites its verification columns), checked before any Graph call or Dataverse write.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §11">Scope: entity-set names and privilege names. Never derive a set name by pluralizing a logical name: a wrong set name fails closed as a denial and hides the bug. Use `RegardingNameFields.EntitySetName` for regarding records and the `CommunicationThreadReadService` constants for communications and threads. Normalize a caller-supplied type with `ToLowerInvariant()` before looking it up, because RegardingNameFields is case-sensitive while RegardingFieldMap, RegardingLookupMap and TaskActionCore accept any case (a client that sends `sprk_Matter` works today). Do NOT declare a new logical-name to entity-set map. Do NOT add entries to `EntityAccessFilter.EntitySetByType` (lockstep invariant with DocumentAssociationMap) or `SemanticSearchAuthorizationFilter.AuthorizableEntitySets` (widens what POST /api/ai/search accepts). Do NOT use the unused set-name column of `CommunicationService.RegardingLookupMap`. Add `sprk_reportcard` to BOTH `RegardingNameFields.EntitySetName` and `PrimaryNameField` using values read from live metadata, and add `RegardingNameFieldsTests` (the two functions accept exactly the same keys), proven to bite by seeding a key into one function only. Read from live metadata (read-only `EntityDefinitions(LogicalName='...')?$select=EntitySetName,PrimaryNameAttribute`) and record in the task note before writing into code: the set names of sprk_reportcard, sprk_communicationaccount, sprk_emailreviewlog, sprk_document and template; the primary name of sprk_reportcard; and the exact privilege names for Create on sprk_event, Create on sprk_document and Assign on sprk_event (task 130 found schema-name casing, e.g. prvCreatesprk_Invoice). Pin each constant with a test that names the live-verified value.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: template merge parity. BEFORE changing the handler, write a characterization test that pins today's rendered subject and body for a fixture template using one field code of each of these kinds on the regarding record: single-line text, whole number, option set (renders its integer today), money (renders its decimal today), lookup (renders the related record's name today), date-time and two-option (boolean). After the change, the same expected strings must come out of the impersonated OData row (the `_x_value` lookup key and its FormattedValue annotation map back to the logical-name key `x`). The handler must not render with empty variables on a read fault: a fault is a non-2xx response.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: suggest-associations and the Office suggestions route. MOVE (do not copy) `ResolveCandidateNamesAsync` out of `Api/Office/CommunicationsEndpoints.cs` into one internal static helper, `Services/Communication/SuggestionCandidateAccess.cs`, that both routes call. It reads each distinct candidate through `IDataverseUserClient` exactly as task 127 does (`{set}({id})?$select={primaryName}`), and returns the candidates the caller can read plus their names. A candidate whose read does not succeed, or whose type has no entity set, is REMOVED from `Candidates`. Any `Signals[].Provenance` string that contains a removed candidate's id is removed with it. A missing caller context (`UserContextRequired`, no bearer token) fails the request with a non-2xx answer, never an empty list. Do not fork the Association Engine's evaluate path (ADR-045, task 127's constraint). The Office route's existing 404-when-not-captured contract and its Names and FilingAccess fields for readable candidates are unchanged.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-002">Scope: whole task. No Dataverse plugins. Every check is in the BFF request path.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: writes. The G5 pattern (owner rounds 3b and 7): check the caller's rights AS THE USER, then keep the existing app-only write where a server invariant needs it. This task does not change who OWNS the created rows (task 146) or who a task is "for" (task 152).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope: parallel-safe:false zones. Do not modify `Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/**` or `Api/ExternalAccess/**` (CallerRecordAccessProbe is reused as is; its methods are already virtual). Modify `Spaarke.Core/Auth/OperationAccessPolicy.cs` only to add at most one key, and only if no existing key describes the right; comparing `AccessRights` flags directly in the filter (for AppendTo) needs no key.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Scope: tests added or changed. No Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;, no DI-registration tests, no constructor null-check tests. Substitute at the module boundaries the existing communication contract tests already use (`ICallerSystemUserResolver`, `IGenericEntityService`, `IImpersonatedCommunicationQuery`, `IDataverseUserClient`, `ISystemUserIdentityResolver`) plus the virtual methods of `CallerRecordAccessProbe` and the `IAccessDataSource`/`AuthorizationService` boundary used by task 130. Host the REAL `MapCommunicationEndpoints` / `MapCommunicationTemplateEndpoints` in-process (pattern: `tests/integration/contract/Api/Communication/CommunicationCreateRecordThreadContractTests.cs`, a `WebApplicationFactory&lt;Program&gt;` with substituted services). No live Dataverse, Graph or SPE in CI.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project hard gate">Scope: before the PR. Run, in full, not just build: the affected tests, the full BFF unit suite (tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests, which also compiles tests/integration/contract, seam and auth), NetArchTest (tests/Spaarke.ArchTests), AND BOTH integration suites — `dotnet test tests/integration/Sprk.Bff.Api.IntegrationTests` and `dotnet test tests/integration/Spe.Integration.Tests`. Batch 3 (PR #1096) skipped the integration suites and CI found three broken fixtures an hour later.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Scope: this task's PR. State the placement decision (in BFF: these are existing BFF routes; one new endpoint filter and one moved helper composing existing seams; no new service) citing `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`. Measure publish size against a FRESH build of origin/master and a FRESH build of the branch, each from a SHORT path (e.g. C:\wt161m and C:\wt161b), both zipped with PowerShell Compress-Archive, file counts equal on both sides; report both absolute sizes, the delta and the zip tool; ceiling 60 MB. Run `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive` — no new HIGH. Run /conflict-check before the PR (email-communication-intelligence-r2 edits CommunicationEndpoints.cs).</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner 2026-09-30 (binding)">Scope: whole task. No scope cuts and nothing deferred: scope discovered during execution is added to this task. Live Dataverse, Graph and SPE are READ-ONLY during development (metadata reads allowed); every live write and the live gate are MANUAL steps for the main session, using the existing non-admin test users in their current business unit.</constraint>
  </constraints>

