  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Declare rigor FULL. Re-verify every anchor in the background (line numbers drift). Check whether task 167 has landed on this branch (look for CommunicationEndpoints.cs in GovernedFiles and Pending waivers naming task 161) and whether task 146 has landed (does TaskActionCore still write ownerid from OwnerId?); record both answers in the task note. Read live metadata (read-only) for the set names and privilege names the constraints list, and record them.</step>
    <step order="1">Write the template characterization test (constraint "template merge parity") against today's code and confirm it passes before any change.</step>
    <step order="2">Add the communication visibility method to CommunicationThreadReadService (impersonated top-1 read selecting the columns ICommunicationAccessFilter reads, then EvaluateMessage), with its unit tests.</step>
    <step order="3">Write CommunicationRecordAuthorizationFilter with a per-route declaration (resource kind, id source, required right or privilege, deny shape) composing: the visibility method, CanCallerSeeThreadAsync, CallerRecordAccessProbe (rights and privileges), AuthorizationService.AuthorizeAsync for documents, and IImpersonatedCommunicationQuery for the template readability check. Expose it through one extension method, `.AddCommunicationRecordAuthorizationFilter(...)`.</step>
    <step order="4">Attach it to: send, send-bulk, status, archive, suggest-associations, confirm-affinity, threads (POST), the four proposal routes (apply, dismiss, create-task/apply, undo), ad-hoc create-task, tasks/{taskId}/undo, accounts verify, and template render. Keep the bare identity filter where it is today, first in the chain. Correct the route descriptions that say "Auth-scoped via the endpoint filter (NFR-07)" so they name the record check.</step>
    <step order="5">Threads handler: read the regarding record's primary name as the caller and pass it in RecordThreadAnchor. Move ResolveCandidateNamesAsync into SuggestionCandidateAccess and call it from suggest-associations and the Office suggestions route.</step>
    <step order="6">Rework the template render handler: read the regarding record through IImpersonatedCommunicationQuery, map the OData row to the same merge variables, fail on a read fault, and keep the characterization test green.</step>
    <step order="7">Guard: correct the ClaimOnlyFilters reason for CommunicationAuthorizationFilter; confirm the new filter is credited by FilterMarker and passes Rule B (its source must contain a DecisionServices string such as CallerRecordAccessProbe or AuthorizationService). If task 167 has landed, delete each Pending waiver it added for these route keys and make NoWaiverIsStale and the per-resource rule pass. If it has not, do NOT add these two files to GovernedFiles (167 owns that list); list the route keys and the mechanism in the task note for the main session.</step>
    <step order="8">Tests: the closed set in the acceptance criteria, then update the existing fixtures the new filter breaks (CommunicationCreateRecordThreadContractTests, the Office CommunicationsEndpointsContractTests, CommunicationTemplateEndpointTests). Then seed each check (remove it locally, confirm a named test fails, restore) and record each result in the task note.</step>
    <step order="9">Build; run the affected tests, the full BFF unit suite, NetArchTest and BOTH integration suites in full; publish size and CVE checks per CLAUDE.md §10; /conflict-check.</step>
    <step order="10">Write projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/task-161-communications-route-authorization.md: live-verified names, the 146 and 167 status, the seeding results, the task 127 correction, and the manual live gate script for the main session.</step>
    <step order="11">Update TASK-INDEX.md: this task's status cell. Leave the live gate items open for the main session.</step>
