  <escalation>
    <trigger>A shipped client (listed in the background) gets a denial for a legitimate user after this change — for example a user who sends documents they reach only through SPE container membership and not Dataverse Read; a sender whose Associations carry a type outside RegardingNameFields; a user who archives a communication but lacks the Create privilege on sprk_document or AppendTo on the communication; or a reconcile-tab user who lacks the Create privilege on sprk_event. STOP and report the user, route and missing right. Do not widen to app-only or drop the check.</trigger>
    <trigger>Template merge parity cannot be kept for one of the characterized value kinds when reading through IImpersonatedCommunicationQuery (for example a date-time or boolean renders differently from the OData JSON value). STOP and present per CLAUDE.md §6: (a) RECOMMENDED — convert the OData value back to the CLR type the SDK returned before rendering, so the text is unchanged; (b) accept the new rendering and list each changed code in the PR. The app-only ColumnSet(true) read is NOT an option: it bypasses field-level security (task 141 put FLS on contact.sprk_externalobjectid). Do not ship a parity change silently.</trigger>
    <trigger>A shipped host of the email composer passes a regardingEntityType that is not a key of RegardingNameFields.EntitySetName (for example sprk_communication or a non-Spaarke table). STOP and name the host and type before adding it, because adding a type needs a live-verified set name and primary name.</trigger>
    <trigger>Reconcile-tab users who legitimately assign tasks to colleagues do not hold the Assign privilege on sprk_event (check the test users' roles read-only), so the Assign constraint would deny them. STOP and present: (a) RECOMMENDED — land task 146 first (team ownership; AssignedTo becomes only the "for" person per task 152), after which the Assign check is not needed; (b) keep the Assign check and grant the privilege by role. Do not decide ownership inside this task.</trigger>
    <trigger>The live gate shows the confirm flow records affinity for a target that is not in the communication's typed regarding lookups (for example a secondary association stored elsewhere), so the regarding-match rule turns a legitimate confirmation into a no-op. STOP and name the column the confirm flow writes before choosing a different match rule.</trigger>
    <trigger>accounts verify: the people who operate the Communication Account form's "Verify" button (COMMUNICATION-ADMIN-GUIDE.md:145, :447) do not hold Write on sprk_communicationaccount, or the owner wants the SystemAdmin app-role policy (`Infrastructure/DI/AuthorizationModule.cs:362`) instead of a record right. STOP and present both; the record right is the recommendation because the caller's own Dataverse rights decide (owner D1/C9).</trigger>
    <trigger>Task 167's per-resource rule cannot credit the shape this task uses (for example it credits only a different filter vocabulary or demands a handler-internal check). STOP and reconcile with the main session. Do not add a Permanent waiver for any route key in this task and do not rename the filter to fit a regex.</trigger>
    <trigger>The implementation appears to need a change in Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/** or Api/ExternalAccess/** (parallel-safe:false zones), or a second new OperationAccessPolicy key. STOP and coordinate with the main session before editing.</trigger>
    <trigger>Any route here appears to need an ADR exception (for example injecting an AI-internal type into CRUD code, against ADR-013) or a change to an API contract a shipped client depends on. STOP and raise it per CLAUDE.md §6.5 with the required format.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>Identity filter `Api/Filters/CommunicationAuthorizationFilter.cs:13-43` (claim-only, attached bare to about twenty routes, several of whose services already read impersonated). Record-route filter `Api/Filters/RecordRouteAccessAuthorizationFilter.cs:79-` (task 076; CallerRecordAccessProbe RPA; fixed route keys `{entityLogicalName}`/`{recordId}`; 403 deny; reads no body; cannot apply the communication internal-only rule). Finance filter `Api/Filters/FinanceAuthorizationFilter.cs` (finance routes only). Decision seams: `CommunicationThreadReadService.CanCallerSeeMessageAsync`/`CanCallerSeeThreadAsync` (`:779-799`), `ICommunicationAccessFilter`, `IImpersonatedCommunicationQuery`, `CallerRecordAccessProbe.GetCallerRightsAsync`/`GetCallerRightsForRecordsAsync`/`CallerHoldsPrivilegeAsync`, `AuthorizationService.AuthorizeAsync`, `IDataverseUserClient`. Candidate trimming: `ResolveCandidateNamesAsync` (`Api/Office/CommunicationsEndpoints.cs:426-`, private to that file). Entity-set map `RegardingNameFields.EntitySetName`. A search of src/ for "CommunicationRecordAuthorization" and "SuggestionCandidateAccess" finds nothing today.</existing>
    <extension>Every decision is made by an existing seam. The new filter composes them per route. Extending CommunicationAuthorizationFilter instead was rejected for a concrete reason: once that class references a decision service, RouteAuthorizationGuardTests Rule B would treat EVERY bare use of it as a deciding gate, so the twenty identity-only uses would look record-gated to the guard — the decorative-filter shape task 074 exists to catch. Extending RecordRouteAccessAuthorizationFilter was rejected because it cannot read bodies, cannot apply the internal-only rule, and denies 403 where route ids must deny 404. SuggestionCandidateAccess is a MOVE of the existing private ResolveCandidateNamesAsync so two endpoint files can share it; leaving it private would force a second copy in CommunicationEndpoints.cs. One added method on CommunicationThreadReadService (visibility plus the access filter) and one sprk_reportcard entry in RegardingNameFields extend existing types. At most one new OperationAccessPolicy key, only if no existing key describes the right, registered in the completeness test.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Any signed-in user can: email the file bytes of any sprk_document, secure ones included, to any external address (send, send-bulk); render any column of any record of any table into a template they control, and read other users' personal templates (template render); inject a message into any thread and copy any communication's filing (send); create tasks and threads under secure matters and make another user the task owner (create-task, create-task/apply, threads); force app-only archives with SPE writes and AI spend (archive); read the engine's suggested matters for any email (suggest-associations, and the Office suggestions route); poison affinity learning (confirm-affinity); dismiss others' proposals (dismiss); send mail and create Graph subscriptions on any shared mailbox (verify); and probe any communication's existence and metadata (status).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

