  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">POST /api/communications/send: for each of these bodies the response is 403 with the route's one reasonCode, and CommunicationService.SendAsync, the SPE download, the Graph send and every Dataverse write are NOT invoked (asserted on the substituted seams): (a) an AttachmentDocumentIds entry the document path denies at operation "read", run for CommunicationType Email with SendMode SharedMailbox and with SendMode User; (b) a ThreadId the caller cannot see, run for CommunicationType Message; (c) an InheritRegardingFromCommunicationId the caller cannot see; (d) an Associations entry whose record the caller lacks AppendTo on; (e) an inherit-from communication the caller can see whose copied regarding record the caller lacks AppendTo on. Each of (a)-(d) also has a NON-EXISTENT-id case whose response is byte-identical to the denied case, and (a) has an unparseable-id case with the same response.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">POST /api/communications/send: a body with 151 attachment ids gets today's 400 ATTACHMENT_LIMIT_EXCEEDED and no rights query is made; an authorized caller (Read on every attachment document, can see the thread and the inherit-from communication, AppendTo on every association and copied regarding record) gets 200 with the same response as today, for SharedMailbox, User and Message.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">POST /api/communications/send-bulk: an unreadable attachment document or an Associations entry without AppendTo → 403 for the whole request with SendAsync invoked zero times (not a 207 with per-recipient failures); a non-existent attachment id gives the byte-identical 403; an authorized caller gets 200 as today.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">CommunicationService.SendAsync contains no caller-rights check: the PR diff adds no reference to CommunicationRecordAuthorizationFilter, CallerRecordAccessProbe, IDataverseUserClient or IImpersonatedCommunicationQuery in CommunicationService.cs, and a test that calls SendAsync with no HttpContext in SharedMailbox mode still dispatches (an existing test named in the task note, or a new one if none exists).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">POST /api/communications/template/render: (a) a regarding record the caller cannot read → 403, and the response body contains none of that record's column values (a canary value seeded in the substituted data never appears); (b) a non-existent regarding id → the byte-identical 403; (c) a regardingEntityType that is not a key of RegardingNameFields.EntitySetName → 400 with no Dataverse call; (d) a template the caller cannot read → the byte-identical response to a non-existent template (404, title "Template Not Found", detail "Email template not found: {templateId}"); (e) the regarding record is read through IImpersonatedCommunicationQuery — the contract host registers an IGenericEntityService substitute that fails the test on any call from this route; (f) a read fault in the handler (the impersonated query throws) and a missing caller context (no bearer token, or an unresolved systemuser) each give a non-2xx response and no render; (g) the characterization test written before the change passes unchanged after it; (h) a request with no regarding renders as today.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">POST /api/communications/{id:guid}/archive: a communication the caller cannot see (absent from the impersonated read, or internal-only for a non-internal caller) → the byte-identical COMMUNICATION_NOT_FOUND 404 that a non-existent id gets, and ArchiveExistingAsync is not invoked (no SPE upload, no sprk_document create, no analysis enqueue); a visible communication where the caller lacks AppendTo on it, or lacks the Create privilege on sprk_document → 403 and nothing written; an authorized caller → 200 as today.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">POST /api/communications/{id:guid}/suggest-associations: an invisible communication → the byte-identical COMMUNICATION_NOT_FOUND 404 a non-existent id gets, and the Association Engine is not invoked; a visible communication → 200 in which every candidate the caller cannot Read is absent, and the serialized response contains no removed candidate's id anywhere (string search over the JSON); no bearer token → non-2xx, not an empty candidate list.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">GET /api/office/communications/by-message-id/{internetMessageId}/suggestions: the Suggestions payload contains no candidate the caller cannot Read and no removed candidate's id anywhere in the serialized response; it calls the SAME SuggestionCandidateAccess helper as suggest-associations (ResolveCandidateNamesAsync no longer exists in Api/Office/CommunicationsEndpoints.cs); the existing 404-when-not-captured contract and the Names and FilingAccess fields for readable candidates are unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">POST /api/communications/{id:guid}/confirm-affinity: each of (a) an invisible communication, (b) a non-existent communication id, (c) a visible communication whose typed regarding lookup for targetEntityType (read as the caller) is not targetRecordId, and (d) a visible, matching communication on which the caller lacks Write → 200 with a byte-identical `RecordedSignals: 0` body and AffinityStore never called; an authorized caller → signals recorded as today.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">GET /api/communications/{id:guid}/status: an invisible communication → the byte-identical COMMUNICATION_NOT_FOUND 404 a non-existent id gets, and the app-only retrieve is not invoked; an authorized caller → 200 with the same four fields as today.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">POST /api/communications/threads: a regarding record the caller lacks AppendTo on → 403 and ThreadResolver.CreateRecordThreadAsync is not invoked; a non-existent regarding id → the byte-identical 403; a regarding type with no entity set in RegardingNameFields → 400 VALIDATION_ERROR with no Dataverse call; an authorized caller → 200, and the created thread's sprk_regardingrecordname (and its sprk_name when no name is given) equals the record's primary name read as the caller, while a different RegardingRecordName in the body is never persisted; a type sent in mixed case (sprk_Matter) is authorized as sprk_matter.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">POST /api/communications/{communicationId:guid}/create-task: an invisible communication → the COMMUNICATION_NOT_FOUND 404, byte-identical to a non-existent id; a regarding record the caller lacks AppendTo on, a non-existent regarding id (byte-identical to the denied case), a regarding type with no entity set, or a caller without the Create privilege on sprk_event → 403; while the Assign constraint applies, an AssignedTo that is not the caller from a caller without the Assign privilege on sprk_event → 403, and an AssignedTo equal to the caller needs no Assign privilege; on every deny IActionSeam.CreateTaskAsync, the FR-E5 PATCH and the audit write are not invoked; an authorized caller → 200 as today.</criterion>
