  <notes>Sweep rows closed by this task: 7 (send, send-bulk), 8 (template render), 33 (archive), 34 (suggest-associations), 35 (ad-hoc create-task), 58 (threads), 59 (confirm-affinity), 60 (dismiss), 61 (create-task/apply), 62 (accounts verify), 79 (status) — the eleven entries of idor-group-161.json. Owner directives: round 9 (fix pattern: reads decided by the caller's own Dataverse rights; writes pre-checked as the user then app-only only where an invariant needs it; lists trimmed; fail closed; unknown equals denied), rounds 3b and 7 (G5), and the 2026-09-30 no-deferral rule. Not in this task, recorded for the main session: (1) thread rename, pin and deactivate and message deactivate (CommunicationEndpoints.cs:165, :178, :192, :204) gate on READ visibility and then update app-only (ThreadResolver.cs DeactivateMessageAsync uses _entityService.UpdateAsync), so a Read-only user can change them — a sweep "noteworthy" item, not a verified finding; requiring Write may break pinning for Read-only participants of Direct threads, so it needs an owner decision before it is added here or filed. (2) POST /api/communications/acs/eventgrid (Api/AcsEventGridEndpoints.cs:30) is anonymous with an optional shared secret — a different file and a different class. (3) The unused set-name column of CommunicationService.RegardingLookupMap says sprk_analysises; nothing reads it, so it is left alone here. (4) After trimming, the suggestions `Status`, `AutoFileEligible` and per-candidate `Conflict` values are still computed over every candidate, so an "Ambiguous" status with one visible candidate implies a hidden one; ids are not disclosed, and recomputing the status is not in this task. Caching: CallerRecordAccessProbe and IImpersonatedCommunicationQuery are uncached, so task 132's C12 (cached None snapshots) does not apply to those checks; AuthorizationService.AuthorizeAsync for documents resolves through IAccessDataSource, which the BFF wraps in CachedAccessDataSource (task 130 notes), so a newly granted reader may see the attachment 403 until that cache entry expires (task 132 owns the TTL). Latency: CallerRecordAccessProbe's ~1.6 s not-found backoff lands on every denied or non-existent AppendTo/Write check; denials are slower than grants.</notes>

